{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm reviewing the imitation admonishment feature. The code seems to have the machinery, but the JEV noted it as absent in v0.3.0.001, while FEATURES.md claims parity. It might be that the UI doesn't display the permanent distinguishing mark as required, even though `public_view` marks it. I need to verify the UI, ensure the mark is displayed permanently, and enact a scenario to confirm the end-to-end functionality."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:35.427939200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm looking at calendar integration. Currently, `calendar-scan` just outputs a card, but I need it to inform project scheduling, persona responses, and background attention. I'll implement a `calendar:upcoming` computed view, link project deadlines to calendar events, have personas reference upcoming events, and have the steward offer temporal attention."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:37.927650400+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-21T05:50:38.024452Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds\project additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=2 loaded=47 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=37] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm evaluating the available connectors for local execution without secrets. The filesystem, ICS calendar, and RSS feed connectors appear to be the most suitable, as they can ingest from real sources and handle network unavailability gracefully. I'll proceed with these three, ensuring the RSS connector honestly reports when it's unreachable."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:41.269608100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the ethics gate for persona imitation. It needs to evaluate requests, apply admonishments or refusals for sensitive cases like public figures, and record these decisions as `ethics:gate` assertions and gate cards. I'm also adding an `ethics-evaluate` tool to check requests against maxim objections and generate verdicts. For persona art, I'll deepen the portrait engine to create unique SVG variants based on traits, store them as artifacts, and integrate them into UI frames with ambient motion. Finally, I'm enhancing the conversation archive by grouping turns into topic segments and making them accessible via a UI view or API."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:43.373861600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the C-SetBuild machinery for geographic set fulfillment, specifically for tasks like listing cities in Pennsylvania. The core challenge is data sourcing: relying on Wikipedia's list machinery. Without network access, I'm considering fetching via its REST API (testing network first) or bundling a dataset. However, the requirement is for the machinery to *genuinely produce* the list, meaning a pre-canned dataset isn't ideal. The best approach seems to be a specialized connector, C-SpecializedListRetrieval, that fetches, parses, and classifies data from Wikipedia's \"List of cities in Pennsylvania\" page. I'll test network connectivity now. Separately, I'm deepening the C-AgenticProtocol for tools invoking tools, implementing a `need`-emitting mechanism so tool execution can open new needs for other tools to fulfill, naturally exercising competing tool lifecycles and set-build operations."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:46.569478800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm addressing overlapping speech from multiple personas. The current `cmd_persona_speak` uses `subprocess.Popen` for non-blocking TTS, causing audible overlaps. I need to implement a serialized speech floor using a thread queue and lock to ensure only one persona speaks at a time. This will also allow sequential respondents to correctly see previous replies in the chat history."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:49.431868+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining persona-specific art and voice diversity. The PortraitEngine needs to generate visibly distinct art derived from persona attributes, potentially using multiple assets. For voices, I'll enumerate installed SAPI voices via PowerShell, assign distinct voices (with rate/pitch modulation) to each persona, and make voice selection editable. A `voice-catalog` tool will list available SAPI voices and per-persona assignments. If only one SAPI voice is installed, I'll modulate its rate and pitch using SAPI XML or `<prosody>` via SpeakSsml. Voice diversity will stem from distinct rate/volume/pitch combinations per persona and actual voice selection when multiple are available. I'll also write a `scripts/scenarios.py` to enact 12 scenarios, emitting evidence and demo artifacts."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:52.513103700+00:00"}}}}
