{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe C-DesktopShell departed silently, but I'm reconsidering its browser-only nature. A minimal dedicated shell, perhaps via `launch-shell.cmd` using Edge's `--app=` mode or a simple Tkinter window, could fulfill the convention of a separate GUI. This seems cheap and honest to implement. I'm also noting challenges for C-ConnectorSet's owner-scoped connectors, C-FullScreen's UI button, C-SupportedOS's declared absence, C-ExchangeLayers' declared absence, C-LiveConnectors' lack of OAuth, and C-MultiSourceAccess's partial conformance."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:55.128023200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reviewing several conformance checks. CompetingSources can use Wikipedia and DuckDuckGo, but I need to test connectivity first. LauncherTests are easy to conform by adding shortcuts. The confidence model checks (DyadicConfidence, CertaintyPrivilege, UserSetSupremacy) seem to hold, with user-set values overriding source ceilings. ConvergentOntology is already conformed. DeterministicMatchReview is partially conformed via its decision model; adding LLM review is a cheap option. HostAuthority, InspectionSurfaces, TemplateDerivedUI, StewardAsTool, UserFacingPriority, and EngineMapping all appear conformed or have clear paths to conformance."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:50:58.444890600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNetwork availability is the big question for sourcing the PA cities list. If the network is up, I can try parsing Wikipedia's wikitext or HTML, or query Wikidata or DBpedia. Alternatively, I could fetch from `pa.gov` or use DuckDuckGo. I'll test connectivity now."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:51:01.873565100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nIf network access fails, I need a fallback for generating lists like Pennsylvania cities. The LLM could generate them, but that risks invented data. Python's standard library lacks geographic data, and while the GreyAvatar repo is readable, wholesale data harvesting seems against its read-only reference status. I'll first test network connectivity to en.wikipedia.org and check if the local LLM is running."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:51:02.957198200+00:00"}}}}
