{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've reviewed the v0.1 Avatars repo and its skills, noting key functionalities for the F4 items. My understanding is sufficient to proceed; the build plan won't replicate v0.1's design due to identified functional gaps. I'll implement my own Python-based, ledger-first approach in the Meridian style. My next step is to define the concrete build plan, starting with copying version 0.3.0.001 to 0.3.0.002 and then adding the speech floor functionality."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:51:18.904819300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm implementing sequential playback for speech by using a queue and a single worker thread within the `speech_floor` context. This ensures that persona replies are composed and spoken in order, with each new response considering the chat history. I'll also change `speak_local` from a fire-and-forget process to a blocking `subprocess.run` call when invoked through the speech floor to maintain this sequential execution. Voice preferences will be configurable per persona and passed to the speech synthesis system."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:51:21.476459900+00:00"}}}}
