{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm seeing two competing retrieval tools for `set.members`, one from a Wikipedia table and another from a MediaWiki category. Both produce comparable lists, which is good for testing the comparison machinery. A third, local \"almanac\" retrieval isn't necessary since I already have two competing sources and a second competition site with two runnables and one unconfigured source. Now I'll plan the concrete code changes, starting with copying the existing code."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:15.221722+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the persona system. `app/speechfloor.py` now handles serialized speech, including per-persona voice preferences via SSML and a catalog of installed SAPI voices. `app/art.py` generates richer per-persona art, from seeded traits to unique artifact assertions. `app/archive.py` provides a per-turn archive view, segmented by topic, with a new `/api/archive` endpoint. `app/compare.py` introduces machinery for comparing competing tools, normalizing results, and ranking them. `app/setbuild.py` handles geographic set fulfillment using member-retrieval tools. Finally, `app/ethics.py` acts as an ethics gate for persona creation and tool requests, including liveness research and an objection/compliance flow."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:17.726832800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the TTS engine: `engines.py` will use SAPI for voice selection and SSML prosody, with a fallback synthetic-tone renderer producing .wav files. `personas.py` needs persona sources assigned and verification that imitation marks propagate to cards and portraits. `builtins.py` will register new tools, give the steward temporal-attention duties, and manage sequential speech turns. New API endpoints are planned for `/api/archive`, `/api/voices`, `/api/connectors`, and `/api/competitions`. UI improvements will focus on displaying unique art, sequential speech, and adding an Archive tab. `__main__.py` and `launch.cmd` will be updated to support these changes, including a `--shell` flag."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:21.161599500+00:00"}}}}
