{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm adding new predicate namespaces to `governance.py`, explicitly registering \"connector\", \"ethics\", \"speech\", \"archive\", \"comparison\", \"art\", and \"temporal\" to the `PREDICATES` dictionary. I've also updated the manifest and launch documentation in `FEATURES.md` and `LAUNCH.md`. A new `scripts/scenarios.py` will run all 12 suite scenarios, generating per-scenario evidence and a summary JSON. I'm considering adding a `calendar` seed for temporal reasoning and updating existing personas' voice fields, but I need to ensure this doesn't introduce \"canned\" concerns. Finally, `conformance.md` will document the disposition for all 43 conventions."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:24.039626+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm consolidating modules to streamline the codebase, keeping the existing style of stdlib-only, function-backed tools, and a ledger-first approach. My file organization plan includes `app/speechfloor.py` for speech and voice catalog, `app/art.py` for persona art, `app/temporal.py` for calendar reasoning, `app/connectors.py` for various integrations, `app/compare.py` for competition logic, `app/setbuild.py` for set fulfillment, `app/ethics.py` for an ethics gate, and `app/archive.py` for conversation history. I'll also update existing files like `governance.py` and `engines.py`, create new scripts, and rewrite documentation."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:26.994826800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe PA-cities list must be fetched live during scenario runs, meaning network failures will cause honest failures. For sequential chat, each persona composes its response after the previous one is appended to the history, and speech is serialized via a floor mechanism. Voice diversity is managed by assigning distinct voice/rate/pitch combinations to personas based on a hash, with user modification possible via a tool."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:30.064409300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe speech system serializes output through a floor mechanism, rendering SSML with SAPI voices and falling back to a WAV file generator for synthesized tones. Overlap prevention is also a concern for browser-based TTS, though UI cards currently don't auto-speak. Temporal reasoning involves categorizing events by time and linking calendar events to projects via token overlap, with a Herald persona offering these links."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:31.986423300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the persona response generation to include temporal context. If a persona has an interest in time-related topics or the user asks about upcoming events, I'll inject \"Upcoming: <events>\" into the prompt. This will be triggered if any event is within 72 hours and the persona has temporal interest, or if the user's text matches keywords like \"when,\" \"calendar,\" or \"upcoming.\" I'll record this temporal note as metadata on the assistant's response. Additionally, the steward's \"calendar-scan\" duty will be extended to offer `temporal:upcoming` attention and check for project deadlines within 48 hours, triggering `project:temporal-attention` offers."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:34.609204300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe ethics gate for persona minting checks for `imitates` by querying Wikipedia for liveness signals. If the person is living or deceased within 10 years, they're marked and admonished; if deceased longer, just marked; if fictional, allowed. Objections based on maxim patterns, like \"no imitations of family members,\" can cause refusal. Compliance requires recording `persona:admonished` and adding `ethics:gate` assertions. The gate card is surfaced in the UI as an \"ethics-gate\" banner."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:35.580516400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `archive.py` module needs to group turns into segments based on chat boundaries and topic changes, with each segment containing user messages, persona responses, and tool needs. The `/api/archive` endpoint will return these segments, and a `archive:segment` assertion will be emitted on demand. A simpler implementation involves computing segments from the ledger and adding a \"topic-segments\" UI tab, with `archive:sealed` assertions marking clear-chat or end-topic events. Topic segments will include an index, topic, turn count, and timestamps."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:37.412377300+00:00"}}}}
