{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `connectors.py` framework registers connectors with their kind, locator help, and trust class. The `configure-connector` tool sets the locator, and `connector-fetch` runs ingestion, producing source-evidence assertions and a `connector:run` record with status and error details. Honest failures, like unreachable sources, are recorded without `ok:true`. Specific connectors like Wikipedia, ICS, files, and RSS are detailed, along with persona source assignment for composing responses from relevant evidence. UI changes include using generated art for roster portraits."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:39.991491500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe current build details include UI elements like chat persona bubbles, a fullscreen button, and the desktop shell capability. I'm noting the archive tab's API segment display and how connectors appear in the Command tab. The speech floor and its card display for queued/played order are also visible. Given the \"cycle budget: 1,\" I need to complete this build in this session. My strategy involves using heredocs for new files and the edit tool or sed for modifications. I'll start by copying the folder from version 0.3.0.001 to 0.3.0.002."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:41.159868400+00:00"}}}}
