{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm adding new predicate namespaces to `governance.py`, including `connector`, `ethics`, `speech`, `archive`, `comparison`, `art`, `temporal`, and `set`. I'll fold `voice` under `speech`. I'm also considering adding `member-candidate` to `search`. For `app/speechfloor.py`, I'll implement a `SpeechFloor` thread with a queue for speech admissions and playback, recording events like `speech:floor-admission` and `speech:floor-played`. The `TTSEngine.catalog()` method in `engines.py` will probe installed voices using PowerShell, caching results to avoid slow lookups and returning \"unavailable\" on failure."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:45.618631700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the speech functions: `speak_local` uses `SpeakSsml` with prosody derived from voice preferences and blocks with a timeout for serialization, while `speak_wavfile` generates a pure-Python `.wav` artifact from text bytes, clearly labeled as a synthesized tone. Voice preferences are managed via `personas.voice_pref`, assigned at persona minting and stored on the persona record, with the `set-persona-voice` tool allowing for diversity and modification. For art generation, `render_art` uses a seeded RNG based on persona details to determine palette, motif, composition, animation, and frame style, ensuring unique SVGs and assertions. `render_portrait` will produce richer art than the legacy `PortraitEngine.render`. Temporal context is handled by `temporal_context` and `linked_events` retrieves events related to a project."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:48.565017100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm defining a `project_temporal_attention` steward duty that triggers for open projects with upcoming deadlines or matching events, offering a temporal attention card via a persona with calendar interest. I'm also composing a helper function, `temporal_note`, for this purpose. In `app/connectors.py`, I've outlined the `CONNECTORS` dictionary, including Wikipedia, ICS Calendar, Files, and RSS, along with helper functions like `configured`, `run`, and `_http_get`. I've noted that Wikipedia connector functions are reused by other modules. For `app/compare.py`, the `eligible` function identifies tools matching a specific need, and `run_competition` orchestrates tool execution, input normalization, result capture, and comparison ranking, ultimately returning full details for the transcript."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:50.882843100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm defining functions for retrieving and setting project build states, including parsing wikitable data for member candidates and handling category members. The `fn_set_build_collect` function will orchestrate these tools, compare results, and generate a final member list artifact. The overall enactment involves project setup, tool invocation, criteria application, and artifact creation."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:52:52.922343800+00:00"}}}}
