{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"_cognition.ai/compaction","params":{"status":"completed","summary":"Full conversation history saved at C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Roaming\\devin\\cli\\summaries\\history_8a3af073da22472e.md.\nSummary:\n<summary>\n1. Request and Intent:\n\n   Overall objective: Build an independent, local-first assertion-ledger ecosystem under the project harness. The intended end state is a persistent semantic ledger, distinct personalities interpreting that ledger, configurable tools performing useful work, and locally controlled devices/surfaces, while preserving provenance, confidence, authority boundaries, recovery, and honest capability reporting.\n\n   The user explicitly directed this cycle as development-harness direction-002:\n   - Read, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `direction-002.md`, `shortcomings-002.md`, and `prompt.md`.\n   - Consult the adopted read-only conventions at `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`.\n   - Use modify-and-measure from `version 0.3.0.001/`.\n   - Copy it to `version 0.3.0.002/`, keep `version 0.3.0.001/` intact, and rectify the shortcomings in the new directory.\n   - Treat GreyAvatar at `C:\\Users\\kris_\\CursorProjects\\GreyAvatar` as a reference realization only.\n   - Emit judge-accessible evidence under `version 0.3.0.002/`.\n   - Update Cycle 2 in `devlog.md` with the result and session end time, but do not fill the separate JEV verdict.\n\n   The direction’s enduring motivation is to close gaps exposed by the three-version investigation, emphasizing “enactment depth, not new breadth.” The required end state includes:\n   - F1: imitation admonishment and permanent distinguishing mark.\n   - F2: calendar temporal reasoning that affects projects, personas, and background attention.\n   - F3: general competing-tool lifecycle over genuinely competing, runnable tools.\n   - F4: all six v0.1-only capabilities: connector breadth, ethics-gate depth, presentation glass, conversation archive, set-build, and agentic tool protocol.\n   - F5: genuine enactment of canonical scenarios `S-list-project` and `S-personality-create`.\n   - F6: perceivable, sequential, speech-floor-respecting voice dynamics.\n   - C-PersonalityArt and C-VoiceDiversity.\n   - F8: three real, runnable connectors end-to-end.\n\n   Immediately before the pause, the assistant had copied the baseline and begun implementation in `version 0.3.0.002`, writing:\n   - `version 0.3.0.002/app/speechfloor.py`\n   - `version 0.3.0.002/app/art.py`\n\n2. Key Concepts and Values:\n\n   Technical concepts:\n   - Append-only JSONL assertion ledger; corrections and supersessions are new assertions.\n   - Computed truth views; no second descriptive truth store.\n   - Typed values: `string`, `number`, `boolean`, `enum`, `ref`, `list`, `map`.\n   - Assertion provenance: source, claimant, certainty, contextual confidence, basis, time, relations, tags, metadata.\n   - Closed claimant vocabulary such as `principal`, `persona:`, `source:`, `tool:`, `system`, and `exchange:`.\n   - Unfulfilled needs (`need:*`) with templates, slots, candidates, gates, satisfaction tests, deferral, fulfillment, cancellation, and supersession.\n   - Tool-as-data DSL and closed operation interpreter.\n   - System commands using `object.verb` names.\n   - Witnessed, scoped, consumable, target-locked grants.\n   - Bounded decision model with tool-trust churn.\n   - Configurable background steward and user-facing priority.\n   - Persistent personality identities outside the ledger, with ledger assertions representing their properties.\n   - Calendar ingestion and project linkage.\n   - Local connector machinery.\n   - Honest engine/stub reporting through launch banners and artifacts.\n   - Speech scheduling via serialized playback admission / speech floor.\n   - Per-personality generated art and modifiable voice profiles.\n   - Canonical scenario enactment and evidence classification (`enactment` versus `repository`).\n   - GreyAvatar capability manifest as the