ence, not only source inspection.\n\n   Honesty and failure handling:\n   - “no `ok:true`-while-failing”\n   - “no silent stubs”\n   - “no env-dependent silent degradation”\n   - Declare unconfigured or unavailable capabilities.\n   - If the cycle fails, record the failure honestly rather than automatically retrying.\n   - Do not fake fleet install or exchange media.\n\n   Cycle close requirements:\n   - Update the Cycle 2 entry in `devlog.md`.\n   - Fill `Result:` with what was built, where it lives, and evidence paths.\n   - Record session end in `Time to implement`.\n   - Do not fill `Verdict`; a separate judge session supplies it.\n\n   JEV scenario suite to cover:\n   - `S-assertion-input`\n   - `S-template-need`\n   - `S-candidate-ranking`\n   - `S-list-project` (canonical PA cities)\n   - `S-personality-create` (canonical coherent persona creation)\n   - `S-background-present`\n   - `S-competing-tools`\n   - `S-restart-recovery`\n   - `S-exchange-import`\n   - `S-defer-publication`\n   - `S-chat-invocation`\n   - `S-focused-need`\n\n   S-list-project quality bar:\n   - Real incorporated Pennsylvania municipalities/cities.\n   - Broad and defensible results.\n   - Criteria preserved through refinement.\n   - Duplicates, townships, CDPs, or other non-matches retained as reviewable result records rather than silently discarded.\n\n   S-personality-create quality bar:\n   - Persistent identity assignment.\n   - Generated portrait/art.\n   - Generated or configurable voice.\n   - Characterization needs/work.\n   - Coherent and distinct final persona.\n\n4. Additional Instructions:\n\n   - The project’s own direction gate requires sufficiently clarified directions before implementation. Direction-002 is signed and considered sufficiently explicit.\n   - `C:\\Project` and `C:\\Harness` are read-only corpora; cite them but do not copy content wholesale or modify them.\n   - Use direct, adversarial review and do not claim features based solely on code existence if run