{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm rethinking the `build-list` tool's role. It seems it should handle ad-hoc lists, while a new `build-set` tool should manage more complex geographic set requests by triggering the full set-build pipeline. This means `build-list` would delegate to `setbuild` for queries like \"cities in X,\" which involves opening a project, collecting members, and creating an artifact."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:23.700005900+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-21T05:56:24.143499Z  INFO connect_post{path="/exa.product_analytics_pb.ProductAnalyticsService/BatchRecordAnalyticsEvents"}: connect_rpc::client: close time.busy=151µs time.idle=80.4ms
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm registering several new tools, including `set-project-open`, `retrieve-set-wiki-table`, `set-build-collect`, and various connector and archive functions. I'm also adding voice passthrough for remote speech and considering if `speak-enqueue` is redundant given `persona.speak` handles the floor. For `S-personality-create`, I'm extending it to use a create-persona tool, which invokes `persona.mint` and `generate-portrait`. This involves adding an ethics gate to `cmd_persona_mint` and potentially replacing the old portrait engine with `art.render_art`. Characterization needs will be handled by a new tool, `characterize-persona`, to generate assertions and ensure a coherent, distinct persona with persistent identity, generated art, configurable voice, and characterization work."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:25.735249600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the persona creation process. The `create-persona` tool will now trigger a \"characterization need\" that can be fulfilled by either the steward or the scenario script. To simplify onboarding, I'll create a `persona-create-full` orchestrator that handles minting, art generation, voice assignment, and characterization. The `create-persona` tool's final step will invoke `persona-onboard`, which includes art, voice, characterization, and an introductory speech. I'm also updating the `engines.py` TTS function to accept voice dictionaries and build PS commands, and adding a probe to list installed SAPI voices. New API endpoints are planned for status, archive, temporal context, speech floor status, comparisons, and persona art/voice updates. Finally, the `__main__.py` will start the SpeechFloor context after registering built-ins and add banner details for speech floor and connectors."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:28.912259500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm adding a `scripts/scenarios.py` to drive the scenario suite and write evidence. For the UI, I'll add persona art to the roster view, deciding to store the SVG artifact path and have the UI GET it, rather than embedding the data URL directly, to keep the persona dict lean. The remaining work is mostly mechanical, and I'll apply patches using Python scripts executed via `exec`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:31.838279500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm planning a large integration patch, applying targeted replacements across several core Python files. This will involve adding predicates to `governance.py` and lazily importing `SpeechFloor` into `host.py`. After the patch, I'll implement the persona onboarding tool, register new tools, update the steward duty list to include temporal attention, and configure `compose_for` for temporal notes before running the system."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:34.350967300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm adjusting `SpeechFloor.enqueue` to lazily start the thread by checking `self.is_alive()` before `q.put()`, avoiding changes to `__main__`. For `personas.py`, I'll integrate an ethics gate in `mint()` before persona creation. If refused, it will record the refusal and return a specific dictionary, which `cmd_persona_mint` will handle by checking the `refused` flag."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:36.526714500+00:00"}}}}
