{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to add a method to `TTSEngine` to enumerate SAPI voices, caching the results since `ctx.engines.tts.voices()` is slow. If enumeration fails, I'll use a default voice. The voice selection will be deterministic, based on persona index, and I'll vary the speech rate. After rendering art, I'll store its artifact and motif in the persona dictionary. I'm also updating `engines.py` to include voice enumeration and local voice parameters, and `builtins.py` to handle mint refusals and switch `speak-voice` to a floor enqueue mechanism for serialized speech."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:38.434274+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm adding an explicit sequence index to cards and assertions for `fn_serve_response_need` to guarantee sequential processing, as the current FIFO enqueueing already preserves order. For `fn_render_speech_sapi`, I'll have it write an artifact WAV file when requested, but default to speaking aloud, relying on the floor to record evidence. The `fn_steward_tick` duty will be updated to include \"temporal-attention,\" and `fn_generate_portrait` will use `art.render_art` for richer output, keeping the existing assertions."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:40.168411200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm deciding how to handle geographic set detection within `build-list`. While a new `build-set` tool with specific triggers is cleaner, `build-list`'s existing pattern also matches. To ensure the canonical \"list all the X in Y\" scenario works through the established trigger, I'll have `build-list` detect these cases and delegate to the set pipeline directly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:42.680152400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `build-list` function detects geographic set criteria using a regex, but it doesn't receive the `needId` required for fulfilling the outer tool request. Since `invoke` doesn't pass `need_id` to the spec's function, `build-list` can't access it. To resolve this, I'll create the set members internally within `build-list` and call `collect` directly, returning both the matched names and artifact data to satisfy existing tests and provide the actual list."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:44.131423700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWait — the scenario script can drive via direct API invokes, so the chat path should work end-to-end. The steward fulfills tool-request needs on a 15s interval, while the `/api/invoke` path fulfills immediately. For the scenario evidence script, I'll use `/api/invoke` for synchronous request/fulfill, but the canonical scenario is chat-driven. The prompt scenario \"list all the cities in Pennsylvania\" via chat opens the need, and the steward drains it within 15s. The scenario script can post chat, then POST `/api/steward/wake` to force an immediate drain, enacting through the real machinery."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:45.612581100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"oasis-diagnostic","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nPatch 6 adds several new API endpoints for managing connectors, archives, temporal data, speech, and comparisons, along with functionality to run connectors and update persona voices. Patch 7 updates the banner in `__main__.py` to show counts for configured speech floor and connectors. I'll then focus on `scripts/scenarios.py` as the main driver for evidence generation, followed by running and iterating on features, and finally updating the devlog. I'll write the patch script carefully, matching exact strings, and use several small exec patches for easier debugging."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:56:46.497558100+00:00"}}}}
